WEBVTT

00:04.010 --> 00:06.440
The trap broke again.

00:08.040 --> 00:10.630
I wonder if an animal 
or something stepped on it.

00:11.980 --> 00:14.040
At this rate, I won't be 
able to earn any money.

00:15.300 --> 00:19.040
What? "You have the tip reward 
you got in Latom Village"?

00:21.170 --> 00:22.190
Yes.

00:22.190 --> 00:24.050
We should be all right for a little while,

00:24.050 --> 00:26.520
but if this journey is going to continue, 
I want to save up for that.

00:28.490 --> 00:30.510
Wait, Sora! Where are you going?

00:33.620 --> 00:37.140
<i>What could this be? It's faint, 
but I can sense something.</i>

00:40.250 --> 00:42.020
<i>The smell of blood?</i>

00:50.610 --> 00:52.500
What is this?

00:52.500 --> 00:54.610
I sense faint magical energy.

00:55.490 --> 00:56.730
Is it a monster?

01:00.500 --> 01:03.470
It looks a little like this adandala.

01:03.470 --> 01:06.460
"An incredibly ferocious, rare monster."

01:09.110 --> 01:10.510
It's still alive!

01:15.180 --> 01:17.200
It's so weak.

01:17.200 --> 01:18.640
It will die soon.

01:24.160 --> 01:25.690
You must be scared.

01:25.690 --> 01:28.940
When I was about to die, I was scared, too.

01:32.190 --> 01:35.370
I can't do anything for you, 
but I'll stay by your side.

01:44.130 --> 01:45.460
Sora?!

01:51.130 --> 01:52.510
This is...

02:05.660 --> 02:06.930
You're finished?

02:08.110 --> 02:10.280
The way you talk has changed!

02:16.770 --> 02:17.700
<i>This is bad!</i>

02:19.800 --> 02:20.690
Huh?

02:24.310 --> 02:26.050
Is it...

02:26.870 --> 02:28.320
According to the book,

02:28.320 --> 02:34.670
it takes a team of at least five high-ranked
 adventurers to defeat this ferocious monster.

02:34.670 --> 02:37.510
If someone encounters one in the 
forest, there's no saving them.

02:39.830 --> 02:42.110
You're so cute!

02:42.770 --> 02:45.560
Maybe you're not an adandala!

02:48.360 --> 02:52.500
<i>When I'm alone, I can breathe</i>

02:52.500 --> 02:56.660
<i>In a world with no one 
but me, I feel at ease</i>

02:57.320 --> 03:01.680
<i>But I think the truth is</i>

03:01.680 --> 03:07.660
<i>That I've been waiting for 
morning's light to break through</i>

03:05.160 --> 03:13.420
<b>The Weakest Tamer
Began a Journey
to Pick Up Trash</b>

03:05.320 --> 03:07.660
<i>(Where could it be?)</i>

03:07.660 --> 03:10.910
<i>Beyond the edges of a yet unknown map</i>

03:10.910 --> 03:15.170
<i>That's where I'll find a place 
where I can live</i>

03:13.420 --> 03:15.170
<i>(If it exists...)</i>

03:15.170 --> 03:17.180
<i>I'd like to go there</i>

03:17.180 --> 03:20.930
<i>And with trembling legs, 
I take a step forward</i>

03:20.930 --> 03:23.520
<i>I'm on a journey without end</i>

03:23.520 --> 03:25.830
<i>And even if I carry nothing with me</i>

03:25.830 --> 03:27.980
<i>I'll take everything I feel</i>

03:27.980 --> 03:29.940
<i>And pack it into my once empty bag</i>

03:29.940 --> 03:31.760
<i>I'll go as far as I need to</i>

03:31.760 --> 03:33.980
<i>On this journey to find myself</i>

03:33.980 --> 03:36.070
<i>And everything I'm given along the way</i>

03:36.070 --> 03:40.530
<i>Will slowly fill my heart to the brim</i>

03:50.400 --> 03:54.760
<i>Now, I'm not all alone anymore</i>

03:54.760 --> 03:59.680
<i>Because I've met new, dear friends</i>

03:59.680 --> 04:04.430
<i>(Maybe we can understand each other 
because we're alike. Isn't it strange?)</i>

04:04.430 --> 04:07.640
<i>Your bright laughter gives me courage</i>

04:07.640 --> 04:11.900
<i>(I feel like I'm wrapped up 
snugly by your warmth)</i>

04:11.900 --> 04:17.150
<i>From now on, let's stay 
together forever and ever</i>

04:17.990 --> 04:22.990
<b>To Latome Village</b>

04:29.250 --> 04:34.610
<i>Does this mean... that 
I have one more friend now?</i>

04:35.660 --> 04:39.540
<i>If I had more magical energy, 
I'd be able to tame it.</i>

04:41.590 --> 04:44.270
I suppose I should at least give you a name!

04:44.270 --> 04:46.150
Let's see...

04:50.980 --> 04:52.020
That's it!

04:54.860 --> 04:57.290
Your name is Ciel.

04:57.290 --> 04:59.680
It means "sky" in a different language.

04:59.680 --> 05:02.320
Wait. Where did I hear that?

05:04.170 --> 05:06.090
Nice to meet you, Ciel!

05:06.090 --> 05:07.830
I'm Ivy.

05:07.830 --> 05:09.250
And this little one is Sora!

05:17.110 --> 05:19.880
Oh, I sense people.

05:19.880 --> 05:22.600
Sora, hide in this magic bag.

05:23.760 --> 05:26.160
Ciel, you can't fit in there, can you?

05:27.060 --> 05:29.800
But I don't think it would be good 
if people saw you.

05:35.560 --> 05:37.220
Oh, how dashing!

05:37.220 --> 05:39.670
Maybe it is an adandala after all!

05:46.700 --> 05:50.540
<i>That gate guard looks sort of scary.</i>

05:51.220 --> 05:53.370
What are you doing there, boy?

05:53.370 --> 05:54.750
Oh, um, nothing!

05:55.200 --> 05:57.110
Don't go playing tricks on anyone.

05:57.710 --> 05:59.630
<i>That startled me.</i>

06:01.920 --> 06:03.880
What's wrong, Sora?

06:05.980 --> 06:06.760
Stop.

06:06.760 --> 06:07.410
What?

06:07.410 --> 06:09.180
What business do you have in Latome Village?

06:09.180 --> 06:13.200
A friend of mine lives here, and I'm 
visiting for the first time in a while.

06:13.200 --> 06:14.650
What is your friend's name?

06:14.650 --> 06:17.600
What? Um, it's Z-Zoliot...

06:17.600 --> 06:20.000
I don't know anyone by that name.

06:20.530 --> 06:22.860
Actually, um, it's Lizola...

06:22.860 --> 06:25.940
No, it might have been Maklewya...

06:46.040 --> 06:47.340
What are these?

06:48.480 --> 06:49.940
What could they be?

06:49.940 --> 06:51.440
Illicitly brewed alcohol?

06:51.440 --> 06:53.050
You've got guts.

06:53.050 --> 06:54.350
Hey, Vellivera!

06:54.690 --> 06:57.130
What's this? You've found a scoundrel?

06:57.130 --> 06:58.870
Go throw him in jail.

06:59.770 --> 07:04.110
He may be a criminal, but you could 
handle him a little more politely.

07:04.110 --> 07:07.730
In that case, I'll be sure 
to welcome him properly later.

07:07.730 --> 07:08.820
Dear, oh dear.

07:10.450 --> 07:12.790
So, that man was a bad person.

07:13.630 --> 07:15.620
Could it be that you knew that, Sora?

07:19.670 --> 07:21.130
<i>He's scary!</i>

07:22.730 --> 07:23.960
<i>What do I do?</i>

07:23.960 --> 07:27.550
<i>Should I give up on passing 
through Latome Village?</i>

07:31.600 --> 07:32.920
<i>This is bad.</i>

07:32.920 --> 07:35.710
<i>Running away here will only
attract suspicion!</i>

07:44.050 --> 07:44.900
Stop.

07:46.120 --> 07:48.860
I haven't seen you before. 
Whose child are you?

07:48.860 --> 07:50.820
Um, I'm not...

08:04.070 --> 08:04.630
What's wrong?

08:04.630 --> 08:07.840
Um, there's a bug.

08:07.840 --> 08:08.750
Huh?

08:08.750 --> 08:09.860
What?

08:09.860 --> 08:11.680
Shoo! Shoo! Shoo!

08:12.000 --> 08:13.650
Oh, that gave me a scare.

08:14.100 --> 08:15.690
Am I good? Is it gone?

08:15.690 --> 08:17.640
Yes, you're all right.

08:17.640 --> 08:19.360
Great! Thank you!

08:19.360 --> 08:20.480
Of course.

08:22.040 --> 08:23.090
Stop.

08:23.110 --> 08:25.950
So, whose family do you belong to, lad?

08:26.400 --> 08:29.000
Um, I'm from Latomi Village.

08:29.000 --> 08:30.300
Are you alone?

08:30.300 --> 08:31.070
Yes.

08:31.070 --> 08:33.470
You came from that far away?

08:33.470 --> 08:37.540
That's right. I've heard that things 
are tough in Latomi right now.

08:38.870 --> 08:40.910
Things must be hard for you,

08:40.910 --> 08:43.750
but now that you're in Latome, 
you'll be all right.

08:43.750 --> 08:45.120
I guarantee it.

08:46.100 --> 08:48.440
What? There's no need to worry.

08:48.440 --> 08:51.210
If you become an adventurer, 
you'll earn enough to eat.

08:51.210 --> 08:52.390
Work hard out there.

08:52.390 --> 08:53.330
Yes, sir.

08:53.860 --> 08:54.710
Bye, then.

08:54.710 --> 08:56.600
Thank you.

08:57.030 --> 08:59.160
<i>Things are tough in Latomi Village?</i>

08:59.160 --> 09:01.060
<i>I wonder if something's happened.</i>

09:09.900 --> 09:12.000
This village is so big!

09:12.000 --> 09:14.980
I wonder if it's because 
we're so close to Otolwa now!

09:14.980 --> 09:16.930
Oh right! A butcher's!

09:18.660 --> 09:19.580
Welcome.

09:19.580 --> 09:23.360
Excuse me, there was something 
I was hoping to ask you.

09:23.360 --> 09:24.210
What is it?

09:24.210 --> 09:26.880
Is this dried meat from field mice?

09:26.880 --> 09:28.870
It's field mice and wild rabbits.

09:28.870 --> 09:30.440
There's some wild pigeon, too,

09:30.440 --> 09:32.430
but they're hard to catch, so it's expensive.

09:32.770 --> 09:36.400
If I catch some game, 
will you buy it from me?

09:36.400 --> 09:40.000
If it's fresh. Are you going to 
catch it all by yourself?

09:40.000 --> 09:40.890
Yes.

09:40.890 --> 09:43.540
Be careful of nonoshi in the forest.

09:43.540 --> 09:45.810
If you're attacked by one, 
you'll suffer grave injuries.

09:46.470 --> 09:48.070
Thank you!

09:48.480 --> 09:50.870
Please give me one of this dried meat.

09:50.870 --> 09:52.010
Of course.

09:52.370 --> 09:54.570
So, nonoshi show up around here.

09:54.570 --> 09:57.580
Maybe it was the nonoshi 
that broke my field mouse traps.

09:59.460 --> 10:03.650
"While we're in this village, we probably 
shouldn't sleep in the forest"?

10:03.650 --> 10:07.210
That's true. Maybe we should rest 
in the adventurer's clearing.

10:10.090 --> 10:12.130
It's so big!

10:12.830 --> 10:15.760
I guess big villages 
have big open spaces, too!

10:19.060 --> 10:21.770
<i>That supervisor looks a little scary, too.</i>

10:27.690 --> 10:28.890
Planning to stay here?

10:28.890 --> 10:29.760
Yes, sir.

10:29.760 --> 10:30.650
Are you alone?

10:30.650 --> 10:31.580
Yes.

10:32.930 --> 10:35.280
That side over there will be safer for you.

10:37.160 --> 10:38.250
Your permit.

10:38.250 --> 10:39.330
Permit?

10:40.390 --> 10:43.010
If you don't show this, you won't 
be able to come in here.

10:43.010 --> 10:45.580
Um, how much does this cost?

10:45.580 --> 10:46.920
No need for payment.

10:46.920 --> 10:50.420
We're just limiting the number of people 
to prevent potential trouble.

10:50.420 --> 10:53.130
I see. Thank you.

10:55.590 --> 11:01.090
Oh, I was so nervous! Why are there 
only scary people standing guard?

11:04.620 --> 11:06.510
This feels so good!

11:07.480 --> 11:10.480
There are so many big tents over there.

11:10.480 --> 11:13.310
I wonder if they're 
mid-ranked adventurer teams?

11:13.310 --> 11:15.360
I'm glad I found a place away from them.

11:17.380 --> 11:20.160
In this area, there are small tents.

11:20.160 --> 11:22.790
Maybe they're novice adventurers.

11:22.790 --> 11:24.610
It must be nice to have a tent.

11:24.610 --> 11:27.170
You'd probably have to worry 
a lot less about the weather.

11:27.170 --> 11:28.250
And...

11:29.710 --> 11:33.670
if we were hidden in a tent, 
I'd be able to let you out, Sora.

11:36.080 --> 11:38.920
I do have the tip reward I was given before.

11:47.600 --> 11:49.830
"We have second-hand tents."

11:49.830 --> 11:53.570
"We buy at high prices, offer speedy 
assessments, and guarantee quality."

11:53.570 --> 11:56.160
I wonder if I could afford one 
if it's second-hand.

11:56.160 --> 11:57.320
Are you shopping?

11:59.530 --> 12:01.490
That surprised me!

12:03.200 --> 12:05.520
I'm the one who's surprised here.

12:05.520 --> 12:07.930
Please don't scare the children.

12:08.650 --> 12:09.750
Sorry.

12:09.750 --> 12:12.050
Hey, lad, are you buying something?

12:12.050 --> 12:14.610
Y-Yes, a tent.

12:14.610 --> 12:16.680
You don't even have a tent?

12:16.680 --> 12:18.830
Did you get driven out of 
your village with nothing?

12:18.830 --> 12:22.150
The difficulties in Latomi 
Village seem to be real.

12:22.150 --> 12:23.960
What's your name, lad?

12:23.960 --> 12:25.520
My name is Ivy.

12:25.520 --> 12:28.320
Ivy, is it? I'm Oggto.

12:28.320 --> 12:29.960
This is Vellivera.

12:30.310 --> 12:32.770
Mister Oggto and Mister Vellivera.

12:32.770 --> 12:35.440
Ivy, I'm going to take you to a great shop.

12:35.440 --> 12:37.750
It's a shop run by a skilled old man.

12:37.750 --> 12:38.280
Ow, ow!

12:38.280 --> 12:39.890
Stop! You're being too rough!

12:39.890 --> 12:41.380
Huh? Oh.

12:41.380 --> 12:44.240
You're built differently, 
so please be careful.

12:44.240 --> 12:47.160
Oh, sorry about that! Are you all right?

12:47.160 --> 12:48.620
Y-Yes.

12:48.620 --> 12:52.290
Sorry, Ivy. He isn't a bad guy,

12:52.290 --> 12:55.490
but once he gets an idea into his head, 
he's blind to everything else.

12:55.490 --> 12:58.550
It-It isn't a problem! 
Please don't let it worry you!

12:58.550 --> 13:00.540
Really? All right!

13:00.540 --> 13:04.010
As an apology, I'll find you 
the greatest tent ever!

13:04.640 --> 13:07.910
<i>At some point, my buying 
a tent became a certainty.</i>

13:10.610 --> 13:12.440
Hey, old man! We're coming in.

13:12.780 --> 13:14.240
What is it, Oggto?

13:14.240 --> 13:16.570
There's nothing here for you to buy.

13:17.040 --> 13:17.900
You have a customer.

13:17.900 --> 13:18.780
A customer?

13:20.130 --> 13:23.010
Well, now that's a young customer.

13:23.010 --> 13:24.740
He's a child from Latomi Village.

13:24.740 --> 13:26.570
Latomi Village?

13:26.570 --> 13:28.770
I see. That must have been rough.

13:28.770 --> 13:31.250
So, what is it you want, lad?

13:31.250 --> 13:33.560
Oh, um...

13:33.560 --> 13:34.780
A tent.

13:34.780 --> 13:37.780
Give him something really 
inexpensive and really great.

13:37.780 --> 13:40.180
Honestly. What a troublesome customer.

13:40.180 --> 13:41.130
What?

13:41.130 --> 13:44.180
Don't say mean things to children. 
Don't you feel badly for him?

13:44.180 --> 13:46.180
I'm talking to you.

13:46.610 --> 13:50.640
If it's for a child, the lighter the better, 
but then they break more easily.

13:50.640 --> 13:53.530
Would you rather have a sturdy one 
that will last a while,

13:53.530 --> 13:55.400
or would you rather buy a new one as needed?

13:55.400 --> 13:58.410
That and the functions you want 
will change your options.

13:58.410 --> 13:59.160
Um...

13:59.160 --> 14:00.500
Yes? What is it?

14:00.500 --> 14:02.850
If you've got a request, 
don't hesitate to speak up.

14:02.850 --> 14:06.040
Oh, it's just that I don't know 
much about their functions.

14:06.040 --> 14:09.320
More importantly, how much 
do they generally cost?

14:09.320 --> 14:11.580
The price runs the gamut 
depending on the product.

14:11.580 --> 14:12.910
What's your budget?

14:12.910 --> 14:14.330
My budget?

14:14.330 --> 14:18.030
<i>What should I do? Would 
one silver tablet be enough?</i>

14:18.030 --> 14:19.670
My budget is five gidal.

14:19.670 --> 14:21.050
Did you say five gidal?

14:21.050 --> 14:22.740
I-Is that not enough?

14:22.740 --> 14:27.260
I have another two ladal, but I'd rather 
not use my gold coins if possible.

14:27.260 --> 14:28.560
Two ladal?!

14:28.560 --> 14:30.770
How did you come by such 
a large sum of money?

14:31.070 --> 14:33.120
I was given it in Latom.

14:33.120 --> 14:36.880
I found some victims of a monster attack, 
and I was given it as a tip reward.

14:36.880 --> 14:39.090
That was some really good luck, Ivy.

14:39.090 --> 14:42.980
If you received that large a sum, it must 
have been a very dangerous monster.

14:42.980 --> 14:45.570
I'm glad you didn't fall victim to it, too.

14:45.570 --> 14:48.400
If you've got five gidal, 
you can buy a good tent.

14:48.400 --> 14:49.530
How about this one?

14:49.870 --> 14:52.370
It's light and sturdy. The latest model.

14:52.370 --> 14:56.850
Someone bought it, found a woman right 
afterward, and quit being an adventurer.

14:56.850 --> 14:58.880
Oh, you mean Lazy Joya, right?

14:58.880 --> 15:01.090
There's no need to say it like that.

15:01.090 --> 15:05.720
That Lazy Joya sold me this, making it 
a good-as-new second-hand tent.

15:07.540 --> 15:08.610
It's so light!

15:08.610 --> 15:11.680
I've made some improvements, 
so I guarantee its quality.

15:11.680 --> 15:13.720
And you'll be giving him 
a discount, of course.

15:13.720 --> 15:17.610
Yes, though I wouldn't give <i>you</i> one.

15:17.610 --> 15:19.940
Five gidal is the price I paid for that.

15:19.940 --> 15:22.070
You'll never find a better deal!

15:22.070 --> 15:23.190
Are you sure?

15:23.480 --> 15:25.700
I'm sure. A special discount just for you.

15:25.700 --> 15:27.700
Thank you so much!

15:28.420 --> 15:29.950
Then, I'll pay with this, please.

15:31.410 --> 15:32.600
Thanks for your business.

15:32.600 --> 15:34.620
You should put your mark on that.

15:34.930 --> 15:36.050
Mark?

15:36.050 --> 15:41.560
You put a mark in a place that only you know 
so that you'll know that's yours.

15:41.560 --> 15:44.180
It can be your name or a symbol, 
anything will work.

15:46.250 --> 15:48.300
<i>I know! I'll use Sora.</i>

15:52.340 --> 15:55.580
<i>Huh? Is this a memory from my past life?</i>

15:54.640 --> 15:58.400
<b>Sora</b>

15:55.580 --> 15:58.050
<i>I think it's read "sora."</i>

15:58.400 --> 16:00.400
Here's a little something extra. 
Take it with you.

16:00.400 --> 16:01.360
What?

16:01.360 --> 16:04.420
It's small, but it's a genuine magic bag.

16:04.420 --> 16:06.300
When you take money in and out,

16:06.300 --> 16:09.420
other people can't see inside,
 so it'll give you extra protection.

16:10.500 --> 16:12.490
Thank you so much.

16:13.460 --> 16:14.900
What do you think, Ivy?

16:14.900 --> 16:16.790
I was able to buy some very nice things.

16:16.790 --> 16:18.950
Thank you, Mister Oggto!

16:19.510 --> 16:20.660
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

16:20.660 --> 16:23.110
Well, we should get back to our patrolling.

16:23.110 --> 16:24.710
Oh, that's right! Whoops.

16:25.420 --> 16:27.090
Ivy, we'll see you later.

16:27.560 --> 16:28.510
Yes, sir!

16:45.440 --> 16:47.280
It's ready!

16:58.470 --> 17:01.610
Sora! This is our tent!

17:04.450 --> 17:07.760
From now on, we'll be able to sleep 
without worrying about rain or wind.

17:12.750 --> 17:15.730
This is our house, isn't it?

17:17.310 --> 17:19.540
I bought it with money I was given.

17:19.940 --> 17:22.200
And so many people have been so nice to me.

17:22.200 --> 17:24.780
It's almost as if I got this for free,

17:24.780 --> 17:27.780
but even so, this is our house.

17:29.710 --> 17:32.360
Am I really allowed to have all this?

17:35.460 --> 17:37.670
Sora, let's celebrate!

17:39.170 --> 17:42.780
Let's go to the dump site while 
it's still light and gather potions.

17:42.780 --> 17:45.420
This is a big village, so they must 
have thrown away lots of them!

17:48.420 --> 17:50.480
That sounds good.

17:58.640 --> 17:59.890
Hey, thief!

17:59.890 --> 18:00.640
What?

18:00.640 --> 18:02.270
Are you sure this is the one?

18:02.270 --> 18:05.330
Yeah, I'm sure. This tent is mine.

18:06.250 --> 18:08.050
This guy stole it from me!

18:08.050 --> 18:10.070
Give me back my tent!

18:10.070 --> 18:13.760
Could it be that you're Lazy Joya?

18:13.760 --> 18:15.490
Huh? Who's that?

18:15.490 --> 18:18.030
Tell the truth! You stole 
that tent, didn't you?

18:19.330 --> 18:23.120
I didn't steal it. 
I bought this tent myself.

18:23.120 --> 18:28.040
That tent isn't something that someone 
like you could buy, you liar!

18:28.040 --> 18:32.360
Honestly, what kind of upbringing 
did you have to turn into such a liar?

18:32.360 --> 18:34.720
You're so right. It's disgusting.

18:35.290 --> 18:38.370
What is wrong with this kid? 
He's carrying so many magic bags.

18:38.370 --> 18:40.930
He must've put other stuff he stole in them.

18:42.980 --> 18:44.370
What's that?

18:44.370 --> 18:46.180
I've never seen anything like it before.

18:47.940 --> 18:49.690
Hey! Are you trying to run away?

18:49.690 --> 18:52.150
You little brat, I'll kill you!

18:54.030 --> 18:55.470
What are you doing?

18:58.070 --> 19:01.240
Anyone who causes trouble will 
be charged a fine and thrown out.

19:01.240 --> 19:03.980
This guy stole my friend's tent.

19:03.980 --> 19:06.080
We're the victims here!

19:06.080 --> 19:07.330
Right?

19:07.640 --> 19:09.700
Do you have evidence that this is your tent?

19:09.700 --> 19:13.680
A filthy brat like this could 
never buy a tent like that!

19:13.680 --> 19:15.410
That's just common sense, right?

19:15.410 --> 19:16.610
Is that all?

19:16.610 --> 19:18.440
That's more than enough!

19:18.440 --> 19:21.150
That's right! You just do your job properly.

19:21.150 --> 19:22.930
Exactly. Exactly!

19:26.560 --> 19:28.940
This tent belongs to this boy.

19:29.520 --> 19:30.150
What?

19:30.150 --> 19:32.800
What? Quit talking nonsense!

19:32.800 --> 19:35.600
I'm telling you, that kid stole it from me!

19:35.600 --> 19:38.120
Where did you buy this tent?

19:38.120 --> 19:39.780
You don't need to know that.

19:39.780 --> 19:43.280
This is a second-hand item bought 
from old man Lagg's shop.

19:43.280 --> 19:47.160
Now you're just saying whatever you want! 
How could you possibly know that?

19:47.520 --> 19:48.500
Well,

19:48.970 --> 19:51.040
the ones who introduced 
this boy to that shop

19:51.040 --> 19:55.520
were Captain Oggto and Vice-Captain 
Vellivera of the Latome Village Watch.

19:55.520 --> 19:56.090
What?

19:57.050 --> 19:58.630
I will ask you again.

19:58.980 --> 20:01.430
Is it true that your tent was stolen?

20:01.430 --> 20:04.390
Uh, I think I might've been mistaken.

20:04.390 --> 20:08.850
I would like to hear your story in more 
detail, so you will come with me.

20:08.850 --> 20:11.270
No, no. We just had 
the wrong idea, that's all!

20:11.270 --> 20:12.320
There's no problem here.

20:12.320 --> 20:16.100
Unfortunately, I have many 
things I want to ask you.

20:16.100 --> 20:18.150
If you try to run, 
you will be shown no mercy.

20:25.090 --> 20:26.580
Stop it, you—

20:26.580 --> 20:27.580
Let go of me!

20:29.170 --> 20:29.830
Stop!

20:29.830 --> 20:30.790
Don't let them get away!

20:31.490 --> 20:32.640
Take this one away.

20:32.640 --> 20:33.500
Yes, sir!

20:36.440 --> 20:38.200
You're not hurt, lad?

20:38.200 --> 20:40.470
I'm not. Thank you so much!

20:40.760 --> 20:41.920
I'm glad.

20:41.920 --> 20:44.400
I'm sorry you had to go through 
such a frightening experience.

20:44.400 --> 20:46.280
Not at all. You saved me.

20:46.280 --> 20:48.430
How did you know that this was my tent?

20:48.880 --> 20:52.330
Captain Oggto stopped by 
earlier while on patrol.

20:52.330 --> 20:55.600
He said a boy would be putting up 
a tent on his own and to look out for him.

20:55.600 --> 20:57.390
Mister Oggto said that?

20:57.390 --> 20:59.780
I didn't know he was a captain.

20:59.780 --> 21:03.840
And look at how things turned out in spite 
of that. As a watchman, I'm ashamed.

21:03.840 --> 21:05.240
Take this and please forgive me.

21:06.970 --> 21:08.160
This is...

21:08.480 --> 21:10.670
a genuine, brand-new potion!

21:13.310 --> 21:14.870
It's beautiful!

21:15.610 --> 21:17.220
It's a token of my apology.

21:17.720 --> 21:19.420
Thank you so much!

21:20.100 --> 21:22.180
I have to go interrogate that lot.

21:22.530 --> 21:24.660
If anything happens, call me right away.

21:26.810 --> 21:28.840
<i>I'm so glad he's a good person.</i>

21:33.650 --> 21:36.470
And now, we will formally 
celebrate getting our tent!

21:36.470 --> 21:39.240
All right! Eat lots!

21:39.240 --> 21:41.430
Thank you for this meal!

21:44.100 --> 21:47.080
What's wrong, Sora? 
You're not going to eat your potions?

21:51.540 --> 21:54.630
Not this one! That's one I can actually use!

21:57.590 --> 22:00.050
I'll need it if I get hurt!

22:02.510 --> 22:04.200
You can't have it!

22:05.350 --> 22:07.190
Sora, yours are over here!

22:11.000 --> 22:14.590
<i>You are not alone</i>

22:14.590 --> 22:18.150
<i>Open your eyes</i>

22:18.150 --> 22:19.940
<i>That’s the way</i>

22:19.940 --> 22:24.640
<i>You’ll be fine</i>

22:24.640 --> 22:28.720
<i>All of us are here now</i>

22:28.720 --> 22:34.540
<i>You’re something special</i>

22:34.540 --> 22:41.810
<i>Please just relax, and move forward</i>

22:42.800 --> 22:47.220
<i>Because you are here now</i>

22:47.220 --> 22:52.080
<i>The world is so beautiful</i>

22:52.080 --> 22:57.830
<i>This place is full of light</i>

22:57.830 --> 23:04.450
<i>You had countless nights of tears</i>

23:04.450 --> 23:11.840
<i>But you walked all the way here</i>

23:11.840 --> 23:18.160
<i>If it’s dark we’ll be your light</i>

23:18.160 --> 23:27.990
<i>You see the end of this road 
is crystal clear</i>
